===BODY===
          <h2>Typical car recovery jobs</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Non-runners on a driveway or street:</strong> a car that won't start after standing, or has a known fault.</li>
            <li><strong>MOT failures:</strong> a car that isn't road legal to drive to the garage for repairs.</li>
            <li><strong>Garage to garage:</strong> moving a car to a specialist, a main dealer or a cheaper garage for a second opinion.</li>
            <li><strong>Home after repairs:</strong> bringing a car back from a garage that's far away.</li>
            <li><strong>Lower or wider cars:</strong> sports cars, lowered cars and cars with body kits that need careful loading.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>From driveways, car parks and tight spots</h2>
          <p>Many recoveries aren't from the roadside at all. They're from a driveway with a slope, a residents' car park behind a barrier, a multi-storey or a narrow street. Tell us about access when you book: gates, height limits, ramps, or whether the car is boxed in. That way the right truck turns up the first time.</p>

          <h2>Does it roll? Do you have the keys?</h2>
          <p>A car that rolls freely and steers is quick to load. If the handbrake is stuck on, the wheels are locked, a tyre is flat or the keys are missing, it's still usually possible, but it takes extra equipment and time. Let us know, so it's included in the price rather than a surprise on the day.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Not urgent?</strong> For planned moves, send the details through our quote form or WhatsApp, with photos of the car and where it's parked if you can. We'll come back to you with a fixed price and a time that suits you.</p>
          </div>

          <h2>Further away?</h2>
          <p>We also move cars long distances within the UK. See <a href="{{R}}services/car-transport.html">car transport</a>. And if the car is stuck abroad, see <a href="{{R}}repatriation/index.html">repatriation to the UK</a>.</p>
===FAQ===
Q: Can you collect a car that's been standing for months?
A: Yes. Tell us how long it's been standing and whether the tyres are flat or the brakes have seized, so we bring the right equipment.
Q: Can you move a car that has failed its MOT?
A: Yes. A car that isn't road legal can still be transported on a recovery truck to a garage for repairs.
Q: Do I need to be there when you collect the car?
A: Not always. If the keys can be left somewhere safe and the car is accessible, we can arrange collection without you. Agree the details when you book.
